{"id":"a3f29b831d74d9fd","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-prop-back-and-forth.md","title":"Back-and-Forth Argument","display":"prop-back-and-forth — Back-and-Forth Argument","type":"proposition","metadata":{"type":"proposition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-prop-back-and-forth","aliases":["58-prop-back-and-forth"],"display":"prop-back-and-forth — Back-and-Forth Argument","depends_on":["[[58-df-partial-isomorphism]]","[[58-df-isomorphism]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"proposition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-prop-back-and-forth"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-prop-back-and-forth</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"prop-back-and-forth — Back-and-Forth Argument"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"956886494eb436aa\" href=\"?note=956886494eb436aa\" title=\"58-df-partial-isomorphism\">58-df-partial-isomorphism</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"01f4b76e2e096590\" href=\"?note=01f4b76e2e096590\" title=\"58-df-isomorphism\">58-df-isomorphism</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L,p_\\bullet,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N}\\in V\">\\(\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L,p_\\bullet,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N}\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span> (partial isomorphism predicate with two explicit satisfaction recursions, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"956886494eb436aa\" href=\"?note=956886494eb436aa\" title=\"58-df-partial-isomorphism\">58-df-partial-isomorphism</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Iso}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Iso}_S\\)</span> (isomorphism predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"01f4b76e2e096590\" href=\"?note=01f4b76e2e096590\" title=\"58-df-isomorphism\">58-df-isomorphism</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span> is the imported structure-universe operator</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> is the imported typed set-function predicate; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_n\">\\(p_n\\)</span> abbreviates <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_\\bullet(n)\">\\(p_\\bullet(n)\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}back\\text{-}and\\text{-}forth}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\exists p_\\bullet,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N}\\in V\\;\\bigl(&amp;\n\\mathrm{Function}(p_\\bullet,\\omega,\\operatorname{ran}(p_\\bullet))\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(\n\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S(p_n,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L,\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N})\n\\land p_n\\subseteq p_{n+1})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{dom}(p_n)\n\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak N)=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{ran}(p_n)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\\mathrm{Iso}_S\\!\\left(\n\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}p_n,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}back\\text{-}and\\text{-}forth}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\exists p_\\bullet,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N}\\in V\\;\\bigl(&amp;\n\\mathrm{Function}(p_\\bullet,\\omega,\\operatorname{ran}(p_\\bullet))\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(\n\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S(p_n,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L,\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N})\n\\land p_n\\subseteq p_{n+1})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{dom}(p_n)\n\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak N)=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{ran}(p_n)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\\mathrm{Iso}_S\\!\\left(\n\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}p_n,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mere existence of an increasing chain of partial isomorphisms is\ninsufficient (the constantly empty chain is a counterexample).  The two\ncoverage clauses are the formal “forth” and “back” requirements.</li>\n<li>Every stage uses the same two satisfaction recursions, matching the imported eight-place partial-isomorphism predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-partial-isomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"956886494eb436aa","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-partial-isomorphism]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-isomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"01f4b76e2e096590","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-isomorphism]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-partial-isomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"956886494eb436aa","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S\\subseteq V^8$ (partial isomorphism predicate with two explicit satisfaction recursions, see [[58-df-partial-isomorphism]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-isomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"01f4b76e2e096590","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Iso}_S$ (isomorphism predicate, see [[58-df-isomorphism]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L,p_\\bullet,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N}\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S\\subseteq V^8","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Iso}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Univ}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"p_n","display":false},{"tex":"p_\\bullet(n)","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}back\\text{-}and\\text{-}forth}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\exists p_\\bullet,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N}\\in V\\;\\bigl(&\n\\mathrm{Function}(p_\\bullet,\\omega,\\operatorname{ran}(p_\\bullet))\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(\n\\mathrm{PartialIso}_S(p_n,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L,\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak M},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathfrak N},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathfrak N})\n\\land p_n\\subseteq p_{n+1})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{dom}(p_n)\n\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak N)=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}\\operatorname{ran}(p_n)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\\\\n\\to{}&\\mathrm{Iso}_S\\!\\left(\n\\bigcup_{n\\in\\omega}p_n,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,\\mathcal L\\right).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":2169,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3932","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-prop-back-and-forth.md|58-prop-back-and-forth]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["956886494eb436aa","01f4b76e2e096590","36d7463d215be751"]}